==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʷʰen-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|gunne}}, {{m|enm|gonne}}, from {{m|enm||Lady Gunilda}}, a huge [[crossbow]] with a powerful shot, with the second part of the term being of Old Norse origin. It was later used to denote firearms. The name [[Gunnhildr]] and its multiple variations are derived from {{der|en|non|gunnr||battle, war}} + {{m|non|hildr||battle}}, which makes it a [[pleonasm]]. In the given context the woman's name means ''battle maid''. See also [[Hilda]], [[Gunilda]], [[Gunhild]], [[Gunhilda]], [[Gunnhildr]].

