====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[device#Noun|device]] for [[project#Verb|project]]ing a hard object very [[forcefully#Adverb|forcefully]]; a [[firearm#Noun|firearm]] or [[cannon#Noun|cannon]].
#* {{RQ:Jefferies Amateur Poacher|chapter=1|passage=They burned the old '''gun''' that used to stand in the dark corner up in the garret, close to the stuffed fox that always grinned so fiercely. Perhaps the reason why he seemed in such a ghastly rage was that he did not come by his death fairly. Otherwise his pelt would not have been so perfect.}}
#* '''2018 February 23''', {{w|Richard Ayoade}}, ''{{w|The Last Leg}}'', Season 14, Episode 5:
#*: Well, I've always been [[progun]], you know that. It's... yeah, I think adding more '''guns''' into a situation is obviously the way to prevent shooting. I think in a way, if we take the '''guns''' away, the shootings may escalate. And I think that's why {{w|Donald Trump|he}}'s so firm on literally [[arming]] everyone. I think if you don't have a '''gun''' in your hands... well, let's not find out what that world would be.
#: {{ux|en|'''Guns''' were considered improvements of [[crossbow]]s and [[catapult]]s.}}
#: {{ux|en|Looking for wild meat to fill his family's freezer for the winter, the young man quietly raised up his '''gun''' at the approaching deer.}}
## A very portable, short firearm, for hand use, which fires [[bullet]]s or [[projectile]]s, such as a [[handgun]], [[revolver]], [[pistol]]{{,}} or [[Derringer]].
## A less portable, long firearm that fires bullets or projectiles; a [[rifle]], either manual, [[automatic]] or [[semi-automatic]]; a [[flintlock]], [[musket]] or [[shotgun]].
## {{lb|en|military}} A cannon with relatively long [[barrel]], operating with relatively low angle of [[fire]], and having a high [[muzzle velocity]].<ref name="jp102">JP 1-02. ''Department of Defense Dictionary of Military and Associated Terms, 8 November 2010 (As Amended Through 15 March 2012)'', p.142. ([//www.dtic.mil/doctrine/dod_dictionary/ Searchable online version])</ref>
## {{lb|en|military}} A cannon with a 6-inch/155mm minimum [[nominal]] [[bore]] diameter and tube length 30 [[caliber]]s or more. See also: [[howitzer]]; [[mortar]].<ref name="jp102"/>
## {{lb|en|figurative}} A firearm or cannon used for saluting or signalling.<sup>{{w|21-gun salute}}</sup>
##* {{RQ:Weyman Chippinge Borough|I|01|passage=It was April 22, 1831, and a young man was walking down Whitehall in the direction of Parliament Street.{{nb...}}. He halted opposite the Privy Gardens, and, with his face turned skywards, listened until the sound of the Tower '''guns''' smote again on the ear and dispelled his doubts.}}
# A [[device#Noun|device]] operated by a [[trigger#Noun|trigger]] and acting in a manner similar to a firearm.
## Any implement designed to fire a projectile from a [[tube]].
##: {{ux|en|air-pressure [[pellet gun|pellet '''gun''']]}}
##: {{ux|en|zip'''gun'''}}
##: {{ux|en|[[nail gun|nail '''gun''']]}}
## A device or tool that projects a substance.
##: {{ux|en|[[squirt gun|squirt '''gun''']]}}
##: {{ux|en|[[spray '''gun''']]}}
##: {{ux|en|[[grease '''gun''']]}}
## A device or tool that [[apply#Verb|applies]] something rather than projecting it.
##: {{ux|en|a {{w|rivet gun|rivet '''gun'''}}}}
##: {{ux|en|{{w|screw gun|screw '''gun'''}}}}
##: {{ux|en|a price-label '''gun'''}}
# {{lb|en|surfing}} A long [[surfboard]] designed for [[surfing]] big [[wave]]s (not the same as a [[longboard]], a gun has a pointed nose and is generally a little narrower).
#* '''2000''', Drew Kampion, [http://www.surfline.com/surfaz/surfaz.cfm?id=766 surfline.com]
#*: by the winter of 1962, the Brewer Surfboards Hawaii '''gun''' was the most in-demand big-wave equipment on the North Shore.
# {{lb|en|cellular automata}} A pattern that "fires" out other patterns.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=Gary William Flake|title=The computational beauty of nature|passage=The glider '''gun''' on the bottom of the NOT circuit emits a continuous stream of gliders, while the data stream source emits a glider only when there is a value of 1 in the stream{{...}}.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=2007-02-23|author=Frank|title=Life on the Edge|newsgroup=comp.theory.cell-automata|url=https://groups.google.com/g/comp.theory.cell-automata/c/DijjKr2p53o/m/8VqQgQzicRcJ|text=It would be especially interesting if someone can find an "airplane '''gun'''", which generates airplanes at regular intervals.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2010|author=Andrew Adamatzky|title=Game of Life Cellular Automata|page=74
|passage=Greene's period-416 2''c''/5 spaceship '''gun'''}}
# {{rfv-sense|en}} {{lb|en|colloquial|metonym}} A person who carries or uses a [[rifle]], [[shotgun]] or [[handgun]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=October 31, 2019|author=A. A. Dowd|work=AV Club|title=Martin Scorsese and Robert De Niro reunite for one last gripping crime epic, ''The Irishman''|url=https://film.avclub.com/martin-scorsese-and-robert-de-niro-reunite-for-one-last-1839491726|passage=De Niro plays Frank Sheeran, the real-life South Philly truck driver who moonlighted, over the second half of the 20th century, as a hired '''gun''' for the mafia.}}
# {{lb|en|television}} An [[electron gun]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Brand Fortner; Theodore E. Meyer|title=Number by Colors|page=202|passage=The problem is figuring out how to get the electrons from the red '''gun''' to hit only the red phosphors, the electrons from the blue '''gun''' to hit only the blue phosphors, and so on.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial|usually|in the plural}} The [[biceps]].
# {{lb|en|nautical|in the plural}} Violent blasts of wind.
# {{rfv-sense|en}} {{lb|en|colloquial}} An expert.
# {{lb|en|Australia|slang|}} Someone excellent, surpassingly wonderful, or cool.

